PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L08U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":8,"cefr":"B2a","unit":1,"theme":"Leaders and Leadership","essential_question":"What makes someone a great leader?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1","title":"They Had Been Living on the Ice for Months: Narrative Tenses and the Past Perfect Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to tell a story with the past simple, past continuous, past perfect and past perfect continuous.","Students will be able to use had been + -ing to show how long an action had continued before a past moment.","I can say \"They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.\"","I can use four past tenses in one story."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من رواية قصة بالماضي البسيط والماضي المستمر والماضي التام والماضي التام المستمر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام had been + ing لبيان مدة استمرار حدث قبل لحظة في الماضي.","أستطيع أن أقول They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.","أستطيع أن أستخدم أربعة أزمنة ماضية في قصة واحدة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"expedition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən/","definition":"a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place","arabic":"بعثة استكشافية","example":"The expedition to the South Pole took two years.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"crew","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kru/","definition":"all the people who work on a ship, plane or team","arabic":"طاقم","example":"The captain and his crew sailed through the storm.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"survive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɚˈvaɪv/","definition":"to stay alive through a dangerous situation","arabic":"ينجو / يبقى على قيد الحياة","example":"All the climbers survived the avalanche.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"courage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɝədʒ/","definition":"the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you","arabic":"شجاعة","example":"It takes courage to admit a mistake.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Stories use narrative tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The ship sank. The past continuous gives the background or an action in progress when something happened: While they were sailing, the ice closed around the ship.\nThe past perfect (had + past participle) shows an event that happened before another past event: After they had crossed the mountains, they reached a whaling station. The past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) shows how long an action had been continuing up to a moment in the past: They had been living on the ship for almost a year when the ice crushed it.\nUse time expressions with the past perfect continuous: for (for five months), since (since January), how long, all day. State verbs (know, believe, own, be) are not normally used in the continuous: He had known them for years (NOT (not: had been knowing)).\npast simple = main events • past continuous = background / in progress\npast perfect = earlier completed event (had + past participle)\npast perfect continuous = duration up to a past moment (had been + -ing)\nstate verbs → past perfect simple, not continuous","examples":["The team had been training for months before the final.","When the coach arrived, the players were warming up.","She had been leading the club for three years when she won the award.","By the time the rescue came, the men had been waiting for months.","He was exhausted because he had been working all night.","After the captain had spoken, everyone felt calmer.","We had been walking for two hours when it started to rain.","How long had your father been working there when he became manager?"],"common_errors":["✗ They have been living on the ice for months when the ship sank. → ✓ They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank. (Before a past moment → past perfect continuous.)","✗ He had been knowing the crew for years. → ✓ He had known the crew for years. (know is a state verb → past perfect simple.)","✗ When the ice crushed the ship, they lived on it for a year. → ✓ When the ice crushed the ship, they had been living on it for a year. (Duration up to a past moment.)","✗ She had been work all day. → ✓ She had been working all day. (had been + -ing.)"],"arabic":"الأزمنة السردية: الماضي البسيط للأحداث الرئيسة، والماضي المستمر للخلفية أو لحدث جارٍ قطعه حدث آخر.\nالماضي التام (had + التصريف الثالث) لحدث وقع قبل حدث آخر في الماضي.\nالماضي التام المستمر (had been + ing) لبيان مدة استمرار حدث حتى لحظة في الماضي: They had been living on the ship for almost a year when the ice crushed it.\nلا نستخدم أفعال الحالة (know, believe, own) في المستمر: He had known them for years."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “They Had Been Living on the Ice for Months: Narrative Tenses and the Past Perfect Continuous”. Let’s learn narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U1-LS1 | They Had Been Living on the Ice for Months: Narrative Tenses and the Past Perfect Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The Leader Who Brought Everyone Home”: In August 1914, the explorer Ernest Shackleton and twenty-seven men sailed from England on a ship called Endurance. They were planning to cross Antarctica on foot. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"In August 1914, the explorer Ernest Shackleton and twenty-seven men sailed from England on a ship called Endurance. They were planning to cross Antarctica on foot.","visual":"Image GV-L08-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Stories use narrative tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The ship sank. The past continuous gives the background or an action in progress when something happened: While they were sailing, the ice closed around the ship. The past perfect (had + past participle) shows an event that happened before another past event: After they had crossed the mountains, they reached a whaling station. The past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) shows how long an action had been continuing up to a moment in the past: They had been living on the ship for almost a year when the ice crushed it.","on_screen":"past simple = main events • past continuous = background / in progress • past perfect = earlier completed event (had + past participle) • past perfect continuous = duration up to a past moment (had been + -ing)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The team had been training for months before the final. When the coach arrived, the players were warming up. She had been leading the club for three years when she won the award.","on_screen":"The team had been training for months before the final. / When the coach arrived, the players were warming up. / She had been leading the club for three years when she won the award.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “They have been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.” That’s not right. We say: “They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.” Before a past moment → past perfect continuous.","on_screen":"✗ They have been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.   ✓ They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"They had been sailing for sixteen days when they saw land.\" Which happened first? … Think! … The sailing – it continued for sixteen days before they saw land. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الأزمنة السردية: الماضي البسيط للأحداث الرئيسة، والماضي المستمر للخلفية أو لحدث جارٍ قطعه حدث آخر.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: They have been living on the ice for months when the ship sank. — الصحيح: They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Leader Who Brought Everyone Home","body":"In August 1914, the explorer Ernest Shackleton and twenty-seven men sailed from England on a ship called Endurance. They were planning to cross Antarctica on foot. But in January 1915, while they were sailing through the frozen Weddell Sea, the ice closed around the ship.\nFor ten months, the men waited. They had been living on the frozen ship for almost a year when the ice finally crushed it in November 1915. The ship sank, and the crew were left on the ice with three small lifeboats.\nShackleton knew that his men's morale mattered as much as food. He had been watching his crew carefully, so he gave each man a job and kept everyone busy with games and routines. When the ice began to break up in April 1916, they had been camping on floating ice for five months. They rowed to Elephant Island, a rocky place far from any shipping route.\nShackleton then made a brave decision. With five men, he sailed a tiny boat about 1,300 kilometers across one of the stormiest oceans in the world to South Georgia. They had been sailing for sixteen days when they finally saw land. After they had crossed the island's icy mountains on foot, they reached a whaling station.\nShackleton tried four times before he finally rescued the men on Elephant Island in August 1916. Not one of the twenty-eight men had died. Today, leaders still study how he had kept his team alive through impossible conditions.","word_count":247,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"While the crew ___ through the Weddell Sea, the ice closed around the ship.","options":["had sailed","have been sailing","sail","were sailing"],"answer":"were sailing","explanation":"Background or action in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"They ___ on the frozen ship for almost a year when it finally sank.","options":["were lived","had been living","have been living","are living"],"answer":"had been living","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"After the men ___ the mountains, they reached a whaling station.","options":["had been crossing all","have crossed","had crossed","cross"],"answer":"had crossed","explanation":"Earlier completed event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"Shackleton ___ the men on Elephant Island in August 1916.","options":["has rescued","had been rescuing","rescued","was rescue"],"answer":"rescued","explanation":"Main event in a story → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The captain ___ his crew for many years, so he trusted them completely.","options":["had known","has been knowing","was knowing","had been knowing"],"answer":"had known","explanation":"State verbs → past perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← الماضي التام البسيط."},{"q":"By the time the rescue ship Yelcho reached Elephant Island in August 1916, the twenty-two stranded men ______ on the island for more than four months.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["have been living","had been living","will have lived","are living"],"answer":"had been living","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the past perfect continuous. Word bank: had been training, had the team been waiting, hadn't been sleeping","items":[{"q":"The players were exhausted because they ______ (train) since early morning.","options":[],"answer":"had been training","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"How long ______ (the team / wait) when the bus finally came?","options":[],"answer":"had the team been waiting","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"Lina ______ (not / sleep) well, so she found it hard to concentrate.","options":[],"answer":"hadn't been sleeping","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Join the sentences with when and the past perfect continuous.","items":[{"q":"They sailed for sixteen days.  +  They saw land. (when)","options":[],"answer":"They had been sailing for sixteen days when they saw land.","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"Hamad led the club for three years.  +  He won the leadership award. (when)","options":[],"answer":"Hamad had been leading the club for three years when he won the leadership award.","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"We walked for two hours.  +  It started to rain. (when)","options":[],"answer":"We had been walking for two hours when it started to rain.","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Tell short stories.","items":[{"q":"Something you had been doing for a long time when something surprising happened: ___","options":[],"answer":"I had been waiting at the bus stop for forty minutes when my uncle drove past and stopped.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Why you were tired one day (had been + -ing): ___","options":[],"answer":"I was tired because I had been studying for my exams all night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that had already happened when you arrived somewhere: ___","options":[],"answer":"When I arrived at the party, everyone had already eaten.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A background sentence with the past continuous: ___","options":[],"answer":"It was raining, and the streets were shining under the lights.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A question with How long had…been…?: ___","options":[],"answer":"How long had your grandfather been working as a teacher when he retired?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: A leadership story.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 background sentences for a story about a team leader (past continuous).","options":[],"answer":"The sun was setting, and the players were sitting silently in the changing room.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with the past perfect continuous to explain the situation.","options":[],"answer":"They had been losing every match for two months. The captain had been thinking about what to say all day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with the past simple to tell what happened next.","options":[],"answer":"The captain stood up and spoke. The next day, the team won its first match.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"had been sailing"},{"label":"had been waiting"},{"label":"had already left"},{"label":"was walking when…"},{"label":"had been living … when…"},{"label":"by the time… had…"},{"label":"for months"},{"label":"because they had been…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"When the coach arrived, the players ___ on the field.","options":["had warmed up for hours","have been warming up","were warming up","warm up"],"answer":"were warming up","explanation":"Background or action in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"The climbers ___ for nine hours when they finally reached the summit.","options":["were climbed","are climbing","have been climbing","had been climbing"],"answer":"had been climbing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"","options":["By the time we got to the stadium, the match already starts.","By the time we got to the stadium, the match had already started.","By the time we got to the stadium, the match has already started.","By the time we got to the stadium, the match had already been starting."],"answer":"By the time we got to the stadium, the match had already started.","explanation":"Earlier completed event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"","options":["She was believing in her team from the very beginning.","She had been believing in her team from the very beginning.","She had believed in her team from the very beginning.","She has been believing in her team from the very beginning."],"answer":"She had believed in her team from the very beginning.","explanation":"State verbs → past perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← الماضي التام البسيط."},{"q":"Omar's hands were black because he ___ the bike chain.","options":["had been fixing","has been fixing","fixes","was fixed"],"answer":"had been fixing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"How long ___ there when they found the water?","options":["have they been digging","had they digging","did they been digging","had they been digging"],"answer":"had they been digging","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"The ship ___ in November 1915.","options":["was sink","sank","has sunk","had been sinking for months"],"answer":"sank","explanation":"Main event in a story → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The volunteers were tired because they ______ boxes of food since dawn.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["has been packing","are packing","have packed","had been packing"],"answer":"had been packing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"In 1953, after the expedition ______ for seven weeks, Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay finally stood on the summit of Everest.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had been climbing","have climbed","is climbing","has been climbing"],"answer":"had been climbing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"Which sentence uses the past perfect continuous correctly?","options":["They had been row for hours when the storm hit.","They had been rowing for hours when the storm hit.","They have been rowing for hours when the storm hit.","They had being rowing for hours when the storm hit."],"answer":"They had been rowing for hours when the storm hit.","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A dramatic flat-vector illustration of a wooden sailing ship trapped in Antarctic pack ice, men in heavy coats pulling a lifeboat across the ice, a small boat in huge waves, and a rocky island under grey skies; a timeline strip at the bottom with dates 1914–1916. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A dramatic flat-vector illustration of a wooden sailing ship trapped in Antarctic pack ice, men in heavy coats pulling a lifeboat across the ice, a small boat in huge waves, and a rocky island under grey skies; a timeline strip at the bottom with dates 1914–1916"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows expedition (a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing expedition: a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows crew (all the people who work on a ship, plane or team); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing crew: all the people who work on a ship, plane or team"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows survive (to stay alive through a dangerous situation); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing survive: to stay alive through a dangerous situation"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows courage (the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing courage: the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W01","script":"expedition. expedition. The expedition to the South Pole took two years.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W02","script":"crew. crew. The captain and his crew sailed through the storm.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W03","script":"survive. survive. All the climbers survived the avalanche.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-W04","script":"courage. courage. It takes courage to admit a mistake.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-T1","script":"In August 1914, the explorer Ernest Shackleton and twenty-seven men sailed from England on a ship called Endurance. They were planning to cross Antarctica on foot. But in January 1915, while they were sailing through the frozen Weddell Sea, the ice closed around the ship. For ten months, the men waited. They had been living on the frozen ship for almost a year when the ice finally crushed it in November 1915. The ship sank, and the crew were left on the ice with three small lifeboats. Shackleton knew that his men's morale mattered as much as food. He had been watching his crew carefully, so he gave each man a job and kept everyone busy with games and routines. When the ice began to break up in April 1916, they had been camping on floating ice for five months. They rowed to Elephant Island, a rocky place far from any shipping route. Shackleton then made a brave decision. With five men, he sailed a tiny boat about 1,300 kilometers across one of the stormiest oceans in the world to South Georgia. They had been sailing for sixteen days when they finally saw land. After they had crossed the island's icy mountains on foot, they reached a whaling station. Shackleton tried four times before he finally rescued the men on Elephant Island in August 1916. Not one of the twenty-eight men had died. Today, leaders still study how he had kept his team alive through impossible conditions.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “They Had Been Living on the Ice for Months: Narrative Tenses and the Past Perfect Continuous”. Let’s learn narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background), past perfect (earlier completed events), past perfect continuous (duration up to a past moment: had been + -ing) together. Listen to the start of “The Leader Who Brought Everyone Home”: In August 1914, the explorer Ernest Shackleton and twenty-seven men sailed from England on a ship called Endurance. They were planning to cross Antarctica on foot. Look at the green words. Stories use narrative tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The ship sank. The past continuous gives the background or an action in progress when something happened: While they were sailing, the ice closed around the ship. The past perfect (had + past participle) shows an event that happened before another past event: After they had crossed the mountains, they reached a whaling station. The past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) shows how long an action had been continuing up to a moment in the past: They had been living on the ship for almost a year when the ice crushed it. Here are some examples. The team had been training for months before the final. When the coach arrived, the players were warming up. She had been leading the club for three years when she won the award. Be careful! Some learners say: “They have been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.” That’s not right. We say: “They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.” Before a past moment → past perfect continuous. Quick check: \"They had been sailing for sixteen days when they saw land.\" Which happened first? … Think! … The sailing – it continued for sixteen days before they saw land. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"They had been living on the ice for months when the ship sank.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2","title":"Had Done or Had Been Doing? Past Perfect Simple vs Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to choose between the past perfect simple and continuous.","Students will be able to explain the difference between completion/quantity and duration/activity.","I can say \"She had written three reports\" and \"She had been writing all morning.\"","I can explain why someone was tired, dirty or happy in the past."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين الماضي التام البسيط والمستمر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من شرح الفرق بين الاكتمال/الكمية والمدة/النشاط.","أستطيع أن أقول She had written three reports وShe had been writing all morning.","أستطيع أن أشرح لماذا كان شخص ما متعبًا أو متّسخًا أو سعيدًا في الماضي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"morale","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɚˈæl/","definition":"the level of confidence and hope in a group","arabic":"الروح المعنوية","example":"The coach's speech lifted the team's morale.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"resilient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪljənt/","definition":"able to recover quickly from difficulties","arabic":"صامد / مرن","example":"Resilient people don't give up after a failure.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"endure","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɛndˈjʊr/","definition":"to suffer something difficult for a long time","arabic":"يتحمّل / يصمد","example":"The sailors endured months of freezing cold.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"determination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˌtɝməˈneɪʃən/","definition":"the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult","arabic":"عزيمة / إصرار","example":"With determination, she finished the race.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use the past perfect simple (had + past participle) for a completed action or a result before a past moment, especially with numbers: By noon, the volunteers had packed 200 boxes. Use the past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) for an activity in progress and its duration: They had been packing boxes since seven o'clock.\nThe continuous often explains a visible effect in the past: Adam's hands were blue because he had been painting. (The activity explains the paint.) The simple shows the activity was finished: He had painted the whole wall.\nDon't use the continuous with how many / how much or with numbers of completed things: (not: She had been writing three reports) → She had written three reports. And don't use it with state verbs (know, believe, understand, own): He had owned the shop for years.\nhad done = completed / result / how many / how much\nhad been doing = activity / duration / how long / visible effect\nnumbers of finished things → simple\nstate verbs → simple","examples":["By the end of the day, the team had collected 500 signatures.","The team had been collecting signatures since Monday.","His eyes were red because he had been crying.","Hamad had given three speeches that week.","The ground was wet; it had been raining all night.","She had already prepared the agenda when the meeting started.","We had been discussing the plan for an hour when the manager arrived.","He had understood the problem immediately."],"common_errors":["✗ By noon, they had been packing 200 boxes. → ✓ By noon, they had packed 200 boxes. (A number of finished things → simple.)","✗ She was out of breath because she had run. (activity explains her state) → ✓ She was out of breath because she had been running. (Visible effect of an activity → continuous.)","✗ He had been owning the company for ten years. → ✓ He had owned the company for ten years. (own is a state verb.)","✗ How many hours had you been worked? → ✓ How many hours had you worked? (How many → simple.)"],"arabic":"الماضي التام البسيط للحدث المكتمل أو النتيجة أو الكمية: By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.\nالماضي التام المستمر للنشاط ومدته: They had been packing boxes since seven o'clock.\nالمستمر يفسّر أثرًا ظاهرًا في الماضي: His hands were blue because he had been painting.\nلا نستخدم المستمر مع الأعداد والكميات المكتملة، ولا مع أفعال الحالة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Had Done or Had Been Doing? Past Perfect Simple vs Continuous”. Let’s learn past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U1-LS2 | Had Done or Had Been Doing? Past Perfect Simple vs Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: She had read the whole report. • She had been reading for two hours. They hadn't finished the project. • They hadn't been working very hard. How many pages had he written? • How long had he been writing?","on_screen":"She had read the whole report. • She had been reading for two hours. | They hadn't finished the project. • They hadn't been working very hard. | How many pages had he written? • How long had he been writing?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use the past perfect simple (had + past participle) for a completed action or a result before a past moment, especially with numbers: By noon, the volunteers had packed 200 boxes. Use the past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) for an activity in progress and its duration: They had been packing boxes since seven o'clock. The continuous often explains a visible effect in the past: Adam's hands were blue because he had been painting. (The activity explains the paint.) The simple shows the activity was finished: He had painted the whole wall.","on_screen":"had done = completed / result / how many / how much • had been doing = activity / duration / how long / visible effect • numbers of finished things → simple","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. By the end of the day, the team had collected 500 signatures. The team had been collecting signatures since Monday. His eyes were red because he had been crying.","on_screen":"By the end of the day, the team had collected 500 signatures. / The team had been collecting signatures since Monday. / His eyes were red because he had been crying.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “By noon, they had been packing 200 boxes.” That’s not right. We say: “By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.” A number of finished things → simple.","on_screen":"✗ By noon, they had been packing 200 boxes.   ✓ By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"He had painted the wall.\" Was the wall finished? … Think! … Yes. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"She had written three reports\" and \"She had been writing all morning.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"She had written three reports\" and \"She had been writing all morning.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الماضي التام البسيط للحدث المكتمل أو النتيجة أو الكمية: By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: By noon, they had been packing 200 boxes. — الصحيح: By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول She had written three reports وShe had been writing all morning."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"By noon, the volunteers ___ 200 food boxes.","options":["had packed","had been packing","have packed","were packed"],"answer":"had packed","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"Adam's hands were covered in paint because he ___ the school wall.","options":["had been painting","has been painting","paints","had painted twice"],"answer":"had been painting","explanation":"Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."},{"q":"She ___ the report by the time her manager called.","options":["had already been finishing","had already finished","already finishes","has already finished"],"answer":"had already finished","explanation":"Completed action, result or number → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الاكتمال ← البسيط."},{"q":"We ___ the plan for an hour when the principal walked in.","options":["discuss","had discussed three","have discussed","had been discussing"],"answer":"had been discussing","explanation":"Activity and duration → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"النشاط والمدة ← المستمر."},{"q":"My grandfather ___ the same small shop for forty years.","options":["has been owning","had been owning","had owned","was owning"],"answer":"had owned","explanation":"State verbs → simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"Before she became captain, Noura ______ the debate team for two years, so she already knew every member's strengths.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["coaches","coaching","has been coaching","had been coaching"],"answer":"had been coaching","explanation":"Activity and duration → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"النشاط والمدة ← المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the past perfect simple or continuous. Word bank: had been raining, had never spoken, had raised","items":[{"q":"The ground was wet. It ______ (rain) all night.","options":[],"answer":"had been raining","explanation":"Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."},{"q":"By the end of the campaign, the students ______ (raise) 10,000 riyals.","options":[],"answer":"had raised","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"Ziyad was nervous because he ______ (never / speak) in public before.","options":[],"answer":"had never spoken","explanation":"Completed action, result or number → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الاكتمال ← البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"How many speeches had he been giving before the election?","options":[],"answer":"How many speeches had he given before the election?","explanation":"had he been giving → had he given. how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: had he been giving → had he given. الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"The coach had been knowing the players since they were children.","options":[],"answer":"The coach had known the players since they were children.","explanation":"had been knowing → had known. State verbs → simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: had been knowing → had known. أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"She was out of breath because she had run for the bus.","options":[],"answer":"She was out of breath because she had been running for the bus.","explanation":"had run → had been running. Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: had run → had been running. الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Explain the past.","items":[{"q":"Why were you tired yesterday? (had been + -ing)","options":[],"answer":"I was tired because I had been helping my father in the garden all afternoon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you had completed by the end of last week: ___","options":[],"answer":"By the end of last week, I had finished two chapters of my novel.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How many books had you read by the age of ten?","options":[],"answer":"I had read about fifty books by the age of ten.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe someone who looked happy and explain why (had been).","options":[],"answer":"My brother looked happy because he had been playing football with his friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you had never done before you joined this school: ___","options":[],"answer":"I had never given a presentation in English before I joined this school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Leader's report.","items":[{"q":"Imagine you led a school charity week. Write 2 sentences about what your team had achieved (simple).","options":[],"answer":"By Thursday, we had collected 300 books. We had sold all the cakes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what your team had been doing (continuous).","options":[],"answer":"We had been working every afternoon since Sunday. Some members had been making posters at home.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence that explains a visible effect.","options":[],"answer":"Everyone was exhausted because we had been carrying boxes all day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"the crew / wait / ten months (had been)"},{"cue":"the ship / sink / they / live on it (when)"},{"cue":"Hamad / lead the team / two years (had been)"},{"cue":"she / be tired / she / train all day"},{"cue":"they / reach the summit / they / climb / nine hours"},{"cue":"the meeting / already / start / when I arrived"},{"cue":"I / not / meet / him / before"},{"cue":"he / study / leadership / for years"},{"cue":"we / just / finish / when the power went off"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"By the time the guests arrived, we ___ all the decorations.","options":["were putting up all","had been putting up for","had put up","have put up"],"answer":"had put up","explanation":"Completed action, result or number → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الاكتمال ← البسيط."},{"q":"Her voice was hoarse because she ___ at the match.","options":["had shouted three times","has shouted","had been shouting","shouts"],"answer":"had been shouting","explanation":"Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."},{"q":"How many times ___ the museum before that trip?","options":["have you been visiting","had you been visiting","did you visited","had you visited"],"answer":"had you visited","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"They ___ the problem for weeks before they found a solution.","options":["study","had been studying","had studied twice","have studied"],"answer":"had been studying","explanation":"Activity and duration → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"النشاط والمدة ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["I have been understanding the instructions perfectly.","I had been understanding the instructions perfectly.","I was understanding the instructions perfectly.","I had understood the instructions perfectly."],"answer":"I had understood the instructions perfectly.","explanation":"State verbs → simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["By 2016, the company had opened ten new branches.","By 2016, the company has opened ten new branches.","By 2016, the company opens ten new branches.","By 2016, the company had been opening ten new branches."],"answer":"By 2016, the company had opened ten new branches.","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"The kitchen smelled wonderful. My mother ___ all afternoon.","options":["had baked three","bakes","had been baking","has baked"],"answer":"had been baking","explanation":"Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."},{"q":"The leader was confident because his team ______ every scenario before the competition began.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had practiced","will practice","practices","has practiced"],"answer":"had practiced","explanation":"Completed action, result or number → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الاكتمال ← البسيط."},{"q":"When the storm finally ended, the rescue workers ______ for thirty hours without a break.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are searching","had been searching","searching","have been searching"],"answer":"had been searching","explanation":"Activity and duration → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"النشاط والمدة ← المستمر."},{"q":"\"He had been writing his speech.\" What does this sentence focus on?","options":["the finished speech","the activity and its duration","how many speeches he wrote","a future plan"],"answer":"the activity and its duration","explanation":"Activity and duration → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"النشاط والمدة ← المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school volunteer day: Sara surrounded by packed food boxes (labelled \"200 boxes\"), Adam with paint on his hands next to a half-painted wall, and a clock showing hours passing. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school volunteer day: Sara surrounded by packed food boxes (labelled \"200 boxes\"), Adam with paint on his hands next to a half-painted wall, and a clock showing hours passing"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Leaders and Leadership”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects)"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows morale (the level of confidence and hope in a group); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing morale: the level of confidence and hope in a group"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows resilient (able to recover quickly from difficulties); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing resilient: able to recover quickly from difficulties"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows endure (to suffer something difficult for a long time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing endure: to suffer something difficult for a long time"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows determination (the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing determination: the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W01","script":"morale. morale. The coach's speech lifted the team's morale.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W02","script":"resilient. resilient. Resilient people don't give up after a failure.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W03","script":"endure. endure. The sailors endured months of freezing cold.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-W04","script":"determination. determination. With determination, she finished the race.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Had Done or Had Been Doing? Past Perfect Simple vs Continuous”. Let’s learn past perfect simple (completed action, result, how many/how much) vs past perfect continuous (activity in progress, duration, visible effects); state verbs together. Remember these patterns: She had read the whole report. • She had been reading for two hours. They hadn't finished the project. • They hadn't been working very hard. How many pages had he written? • How long had he been writing? Use the past perfect simple (had + past participle) for a completed action or a result before a past moment, especially with numbers: By noon, the volunteers had packed 200 boxes. Use the past perfect continuous (had been + -ing) for an activity in progress and its duration: They had been packing boxes since seven o'clock. The continuous often explains a visible effect in the past: Adam's hands were blue because he had been painting. (The activity explains the paint.) The simple shows the activity was finished: He had painted the whole wall. Here are some examples. By the end of the day, the team had collected 500 signatures. The team had been collecting signatures since Monday. His eyes were red because he had been crying. Be careful! Some learners say: “By noon, they had been packing 200 boxes.” That’s not right. We say: “By noon, they had packed 200 boxes.” A number of finished things → simple. Quick check: \"He had painted the wall.\" Was the wall finished? … Think! … Yes. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"She had written three reports\" and \"She had been writing all morning.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3","title":"Collaborate, Delegate, Inspire: Leadership Vocabulary and Prefixes","objectives":["Students will be able to use precise leadership vocabulary.","Students will be able to use prefixes (co-, mis-, over-, under-, re-, inter-, self-) to understand and form new words.","I can describe a leader with words like integrity, vision and initiative.","I can work out \"underestimate\" and \"self-discipline\" from their prefixes."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام مفردات القيادة بدقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام البادئات (co- وmis- وover- وunder- وre- وinter- وself-) لفهم كلمات جديدة وتكوينها.","أستطيع أن أصف قائدًا بكلمات مثل integrity وvision وinitiative.","أستطيع أن أستنتج معنى underestimate وself-discipline من بادئاتهما."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"delegate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdɛləˌɡeɪt/","definition":"to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else","arabic":"يفوّض","example":"A good captain delegates tasks to the team.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"collaborate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlæbɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to work together with others on a project","arabic":"يتعاون","example":"The two schools collaborated on a science project.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"initiative","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪˈnɪʃətɪv/","definition":"the ability to act and make decisions without being told","arabic":"المبادرة","example":"Faisal took the initiative and organized the event.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"integrity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈtɛɡrəti/","definition":"the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles","arabic":"النزاهة","example":"Leaders with integrity keep their promises.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W04"},{"word":"vision","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɪʒən/","definition":"a clear idea of what you want to achieve in the future","arabic":"رؤية","example":"Saudi Vision 2030 is a plan for the future of the country.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W05"},{"word":"mentor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛnˌtɔr/","definition":"an experienced person who advises and guides a younger person","arabic":"مرشد / موجّه","example":"My older cousin is my mentor in programming.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W06"},{"word":"accountable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈkaʊntəbəl/","definition":"responsible for your actions and expected to explain them","arabic":"مسؤول / خاضع للمساءلة","example":"Every team member is accountable for his part.","image_id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W07","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W07"}],"explanation":{"text":"Leadership words: courage, morale, resilient, endure, determination, delegate, collaborate, initiative, integrity, vision, mentor, accountable. Useful collocations: take the initiative, boost / lift morale, show courage, share a vision, hold someone accountable, lead by example.\nPrefixes change meaning: co- / col- / com- = together (co-captain, collaborate); mis- = wrongly (misjudge, mislead); over- = too much (overconfident); under- = too little (underestimate); re- = again (rebuild, rethink); inter- = between (interact, international); self- = of yourself (self-confident, self-discipline – with a hyphen).\nWord families: lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination → determined; collaborate → collaboration → collaborative; resilience → resilient; decide → decision → decisive.\nWord families: lead: leader (n), leadership (n), leading (adj) | determine: determination (n), determined (adj) | collaborate: collaboration (n), collaborative (adj) | resilience: resilient (adj), resiliently (adv) | inspire: inspiration (n), inspirational (adj) | decide: decision (n), decisive (adj), decisively (adv) | responsible: responsibility (n), responsibly (adv)","examples":["A good leader takes the initiative when others hesitate.","The captain lifted the team's morale with a short speech.","Don't underestimate your opponents.","He was overconfident and didn't prepare.","Our school collaborated with a hospital on a health campaign.","Leaders with integrity admit their mistakes.","Self-discipline helps athletes train every day.","My mentor taught me to lead by example."],"common_errors":["✗ He took an initiative and organized everything. → ✓ He took the initiative and organized everything. (Fixed phrase: take the initiative.)","✗ The team's moral was low. → ✓ The team's morale was low. (morale (confidence) ≠ moral (right and wrong).)","✗ She showed great determinate. → ✓ She showed great determination. (After great → noun.)","✗ I underestimated how good he was, so I won easily. → ✓ I underestimated how good he was, so I lost. (underestimate = think something is less than it really is.)"],"arabic":"مفردات القيادة: integrity (النزاهة) وvision (الرؤية) وinitiative (المبادرة) وmorale (الروح المعنوية) وmentor (المرشد).\nالبادئات: co / col (معًا)، mis (خطأً)، over (أكثر من اللازم)، under (أقل من اللازم)، re (مرة أخرى)، inter (بين)، self (الذات).\nانتبه: morale (الروح المعنوية) تختلف عن moral (أخلاقي).\nعائلات الكلمات: lead ← leader ← leadership، وdetermine ← determination ← determined."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Collaborate, Delegate, Inspire: Leadership Vocabulary and Prefixes”. Let’s learn leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U1-LS3 | Collaborate, Delegate, Inspire: Leadership Vocabulary and Prefixes","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. delegate: to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else. collaborate: to work together with others on a project. initiative: the ability to act and make decisions without being told.","on_screen":"delegate | collaborate | initiative","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Leadership words: courage, morale, resilient, endure, determination, delegate, collaborate, initiative, integrity, vision, mentor, accountable. Useful collocations: take the initiative, boost / lift morale, show courage, share a vision, hold someone accountable, lead by example. Prefixes change meaning: co- / col- / com- = together (co-captain, collaborate); mis- = wrongly (misjudge, mislead); over- = too much (overconfident); under- = too little (underestimate); re- = again (rebuild, rethink); inter- = between (interact, international); self- = of yourself (self-confident, self-discipline – with a hyphen).","on_screen":"leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self-","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. A good leader takes the initiative when others hesitate. The captain lifted the team's morale with a short speech. Don't underestimate your opponents.","on_screen":"A good leader takes the initiative when others hesitate. / The captain lifted the team's morale with a short speech. / Don't underestimate your opponents.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He took an initiative and organized everything.” That’s not right. We say: “He took the initiative and organized everything.” Fixed phrase: take the initiative.","on_screen":"✗ He took an initiative and organized everything.   ✓ He took the initiative and organized everything.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: If you \"underestimate\" a task, do you think it is easier or harder than it really is? … Think! … Easier. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a leader with words like integrity, vision and initiative.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a leader with words like integrity, vision and initiative.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self-.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","مفردات القيادة: integrity (النزاهة) وvision (الرؤية) وinitiative (المبادرة) وmorale (الروح المعنوية) وmentor (المرشد).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He took an initiative and organized everything. — الصحيح: He took the initiative and organized everything.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف قائدًا بكلمات مثل integrity وvision وinitiative."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The captain's calm speech lifted the team's ___.","options":["vision","moral","mentor","morale"],"answer":"morale","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Faisal didn't wait for instructions; he took the ___.","options":["crew","expedition","initiative","integrity"],"answer":"initiative","explanation":"Leadership collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"Don't ___ your opponents. They're better than you think.","options":["interact","overestimate","misbehave","underestimate"],"answer":"underestimate","explanation":"Use the prefix to find or form the meaning.","explanation_ar":"البادئة."},{"q":"Hamad's ___ to win inspired the whole team.","options":["determination","determine","determinedly","determined"],"answer":"determination","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"A leader with ___ is honest and keeps his promises.","options":["initiative","integrity","morale","expedition"],"answer":"integrity","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Many athletes are ______; they recover from injuries and losses and return even stronger.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["anonymous","careless","resilient","reluctant"],"answer":"resilient","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the prefix word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"co-captain","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"a person who leads a team together with another captain","explanation":"co-captain → a person who leads a team together with another captain. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"misjudge","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"to form a wrong opinion about someone","explanation":"misjudge → to form a wrong opinion about someone. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"overconfident","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"too sure of yourself","explanation":"overconfident → too sure of yourself. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"rebuild","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"to build something again","explanation":"rebuild → to build something again. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"international","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"between different countries","explanation":"international → between different countries. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"self-discipline","options":["a person who leads a team together with another captain","to build something again","between different countries","too sure of yourself","the ability to control yourself and work hard","to form a wrong opinion about someone"],"answer":"the ability to control yourself and work hard","explanation":"self-discipline → the ability to control yourself and work hard. Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about leadership.","items":[{"q":"Describe a leader you admire with two words from the unit.","options":[],"answer":"My grandfather is a leader with integrity and vision.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A time you took the initiative: ___","options":[],"answer":"I took the initiative and organized a cleanup of our street.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A task you once underestimated: ___","options":[],"answer":"I underestimated my science project; it took three weeks, not three days.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who is your mentor, and what has he or she taught you?","options":[],"answer":"My uncle is my mentor; he has taught me to manage my time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"collaborate\".","options":[],"answer":"Our class collaborated with a school in Riyadh on a video project.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Leadership qualities poster.","items":[{"q":"Write the 3 most important qualities of a leader and explain each.","options":[],"answer":"Integrity – people trust you. Vision – you know where you're going. Resilience – you don't give up.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with prefix words (over-, under-, mis-, re-, self-).","options":[],"answer":"A good leader is self-confident but not overconfident. He rethinks his plans when things go wrong.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about how a leader can boost morale.","options":[],"answer":"A leader can boost morale by thanking every team member.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"leader","category":"noun","family":"lead"},{"word":"leadership","category":"noun","family":"lead"},{"word":"leading","category":"adjective","family":"lead"},{"word":"determination","category":"noun","family":"determine"},{"word":"determined","category":"adjective","family":"determine"},{"word":"collaboration","category":"noun","family":"collaborate"},{"word":"collaborative","category":"adjective","family":"collaborate"},{"word":"resilient","category":"adjective","family":"resilience"},{"word":"resiliently","category":"adverb","family":"resilience"},{"word":"inspiration","category":"noun","family":"inspire"},{"word":"inspirational","category":"adjective","family":"inspire"},{"word":"decision","category":"noun","family":"decide"},{"word":"decisive","category":"adjective","family":"decide"},{"word":"decisively","category":"adverb","family":"decide"},{"word":"responsibility","category":"noun","family":"responsible"},{"word":"responsibly","category":"adverb","family":"responsible"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Our school ___ with a local hospital on a health awareness project.","options":["delegated","collaborated","misled","endured"],"answer":"collaborated","explanation":"Leadership collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"A good manager ___ some tasks to his team instead of doing everything himself.","options":["delegates","survives","collaborates","endures"],"answer":"delegates","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The advertisement ___ customers; the product wasn't as good as it said.","options":["reled","underled","misled","overled"],"answer":"misled","explanation":"Use the prefix to find or form the meaning.","explanation_ar":"البادئة."},{"q":"She is a natural ___; people follow her without being asked.","options":["lead","leader","leadership","leading"],"answer":"leader","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The judges praised the team's ___ approach to solving problems.","options":["collaborate","collaborator","collaboration","collaborative"],"answer":"collaborative","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The sailors had to ___ terrible storms for weeks.","options":["endure","delegate","collaborate","mentor"],"answer":"endure","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The coach holds every player ___ for his own fitness.","options":["accountably","accounting","accountant","accountable"],"answer":"accountable","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Students from twenty countries attended the ___ science fair.","options":["intranational","international","internation","interational"],"answer":"international","explanation":"Use the prefix to find or form the meaning.","explanation_ar":"البادئة."},{"q":"Although the young engineer had little experience, her clear ______ for the project—a cheaper, solar-powered water pump—convinced the investors.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["vision","expedition","crew","morale"],"answer":"vision","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"After the earthquake, the community worked together to ______ the damaged school within a year.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["misbuild","interbuild","rebuild","overbuild"],"answer":"rebuild","explanation":"Use the prefix to find or form the meaning.","explanation_ar":"البادئة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A \"Leadership Toolbox\" poster: icons for vision (a telescope), integrity (a balance), initiative (a lightning bolt), collaboration (two hands joining puzzle pieces), mentor (an older and a younger student walking together); prefix cards co-, mis-, over-, under-, re-, inter-, self- hanging from a line. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A \"Leadership Toolbox\" poster: icons for vision (a telescope), integrity (a balance), initiative (a lightning bolt), collaboration (two hands joining puzzle pieces), mentor (an older and a younger student walking together); prefix cards co-, mis-, over-, under-, re-, inter-, self- hanging from a line"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 7 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows delegate (to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing delegate: to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows collaborate (to work together with others on a project); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing collaborate: to work together with others on a project"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows initiative (the ability to act and make decisions without being told); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing initiative: the ability to act and make decisions without being told"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows integrity (the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing integrity: the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vision (a clear idea of what you want to achieve in the future); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vision: a clear idea of what you want to achieve in the future"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mentor (an experienced person who advises and guides a younger person); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mentor: an experienced person who advises and guides a younger person"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-W07","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows accountable (responsible for your actions and expected to explain them); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing accountable: responsible for your actions and expected to explain them"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W01","script":"delegate. delegate. A good captain delegates tasks to the team.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W02","script":"collaborate. collaborate. The two schools collaborated on a science project.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W03","script":"initiative. initiative. Faisal took the initiative and organized the event.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W04","script":"integrity. integrity. Leaders with integrity keep their promises.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W05","script":"vision. vision. Saudi Vision 2030 is a plan for the future of the country.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W06","script":"mentor. mentor. My older cousin is my mentor in programming.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-W07","script":"accountable. accountable. Every team member is accountable for his part.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Collaborate, Delegate, Inspire: Leadership Vocabulary and Prefixes”. Let’s learn leadership vocabulary; word families (lead → leader → leadership; determine → determination); prefixes co-/col-, mis-, over-/under-, re-, inter-, self- together. Meet some new words. delegate: to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else. collaborate: to work together with others on a project. initiative: the ability to act and make decisions without being told. Leadership words: courage, morale, resilient, endure, determination, delegate, collaborate, initiative, integrity, vision, mentor, accountable. Useful collocations: take the initiative, boost / lift morale, show courage, share a vision, hold someone accountable, lead by example. Prefixes change meaning: co- / col- / com- = together (co-captain, collaborate); mis- = wrongly (misjudge, mislead); over- = too much (overconfident); under- = too little (underestimate); re- = again (rebuild, rethink); inter- = between (interact, international); self- = of yourself (self-confident, self-discipline – with a hyphen). Here are some examples. A good leader takes the initiative when others hesitate. The captain lifted the team's morale with a short speech. Don't underestimate your opponents. Be careful! Some learners say: “He took an initiative and organized everything.” That’s not right. We say: “He took the initiative and organized everything.” Fixed phrase: take the initiative. Quick check: If you \"underestimate\" a task, do you think it is easier or harder than it really is? … Think! … Easier. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a leader with words like integrity, vision and initiative.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4","title":"Fixing Run-Ons and Comma Splices: Periods, Conjunctions and Semicolons (SAT Boundaries)","objectives":["Students will be able to identify run-ons and comma splices and fix them in four ways.","Students will be able to use semicolons correctly, including with conjunctive adverbs such as however and therefore.","I can fix \"The ship sank, the men survived\" in four ways.","I can write \"The ice was thick; however, they kept going.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على الجمل المتصلة الخاطئة وجمل الفاصلة الخاطئة وتصحيحها بأربع طرق.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الفاصلة المنقوطة بشكل صحيح، ومنها مع ظروف الربط مثل however وtherefore.","أستطيع أن أصحّح The ship sank, the men survived بأربع طرق.","أستطيع أن أكتب The ice was thick; however, they kept going."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"expedition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən/","definition":"a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place","arabic":"بعثة استكشافية","example":"The expedition to the South Pole took two years.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"crew","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kru/","definition":"all the people who work on a ship, plane or team","arabic":"طاقم","example":"The captain and his crew sailed through the storm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"survive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɚˈvaɪv/","definition":"to stay alive through a dangerous situation","arabic":"ينجو / يبقى على قيد الحياة","example":"All the climbers survived the avalanche.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"courage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɝədʒ/","definition":"the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you","arabic":"شجاعة","example":"It takes courage to admit a mistake.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"morale","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɚˈæl/","definition":"the level of confidence and hope in a group","arabic":"الروح المعنوية","example":"The coach's speech lifted the team's morale.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"resilient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪljənt/","definition":"able to recover quickly from difficulties","arabic":"صامد / مرن","example":"Resilient people don't give up after a failure.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Two independent clauses (each with its own subject and verb and a complete idea) can't be joined with nothing (a run-on) or with only a comma (a comma splice): (not: The ship sank the men survived.) (not: The ship sank, the men survived.) These are the most common errors tested in the SAT Boundaries questions.\nFour correct fixes: (1) period: The ship sank. The men survived. (2) comma + FANBOYS (for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so): The ship sank, but the men survived. (3) semicolon for closely related ideas: The ship sank; the men survived. (4) subordinating conjunction: Although the ship sank, the men survived.\nConjunctive adverbs (however, therefore, moreover, consequently, nevertheless, meanwhile) are not conjunctions. Between two independent clauses use a semicolon before and a comma after: The ice was thick; however, they kept going. Don't put a semicolon before a dependent clause: (not: They kept going; although the ice was thick.)\nrun-on: IC IC • comma splice: IC, IC → both wrong\nfixes: IC. IC • IC, FANBOYS IC • IC; IC • Although IC, IC\nIC; however, IC (semicolon before, comma after)\nno semicolon before a dependent clause or a phrase","examples":["Shackleton gave every man a job; nobody had time to despair.","The storm was violent, yet the small boat stayed afloat.","Because the captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.","The plan was risky; however, it was their only chance.","The team lost the first match; consequently, the coach changed the strategy.","Hamad delegated the tasks, and everyone knew exactly what to do.","The leader made a mistake. He admitted it immediately.","She had been training for months; therefore, she felt ready."],"common_errors":["✗ The captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him. → ✓ The captain stayed calm, so the crew trusted him. (Comma splice → add a FANBOYS conjunction (or use a semicolon or a period).)","✗ The plan was risky, however, it was their only chance. → ✓ The plan was risky; however, it was their only chance. (however between two clauses → semicolon before it.)","✗ They kept going; although the ice was thick. → ✓ They kept going, although the ice was thick. (No semicolon before a dependent clause.)","✗ The team was tired they kept practicing. → ✓ The team was tired, but they kept practicing. (Run-on → add punctuation and a conjunction.)"],"arabic":"الجملة المستقلة لها فاعل وفعل وفكرة كاملة، ولا نربط جملتين مستقلتين بلا شيء (run-on) أو بفاصلة فقط (comma splice).\nالتصحيح بأربع طرق: نقطة، أو فاصلة + أداة ربط (FANBOYS)، أو فاصلة منقوطة، أو أداة ربط تابعة (although / because).\nظروف الربط مثل however وtherefore ليست أدوات ربط، فنضع قبلها فاصلة منقوطة وبعدها فاصلة: The plan was risky; however, it was their only chance.\nلا نضع فاصلة منقوطة قبل جملة تابعة. وهذه الأخطاء أكثر ما يُختبر في أسئلة Boundaries في اختبار SAT."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Fixing Run-Ons and Comma Splices: Periods, Conjunctions and Semicolons (SAT Boundaries)”. Let’s learn sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U1-LS4 | Fixing Run-Ons and Comma Splices: Periods, Conjunctions and Semicolons (SAT Boundaries)","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Two independent clauses (each with its own subject and verb and a complete idea) can't be joined with nothing (a run-on) or with only a comma (a comma splice): (not: The ship sank the men survived.) (not: The ship sank, the men survived.) These are the most common errors tested in the SAT Boundaries questions.","on_screen":"sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Two independent clauses (each with its own subject and verb and a complete idea) can't be joined with nothing (a run-on) or with only a comma (a comma splice): (not: The ship sank the men survived.) (not: The ship sank, the men survived.) These are the most common errors tested in the SAT Boundaries questions. Four correct fixes: (1) period: The ship sank. The men survived. (2) comma + FANBOYS (for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so): The ship sank, but the men survived. (3) semicolon for closely related ideas: The ship sank; the men survived. (4) subordinating conjunction: Although the ship sank, the men survived.","on_screen":"run-on: IC IC • comma splice: IC, IC → both wrong • fixes: IC. IC • IC, FANBOYS IC • IC; IC • Although IC, IC • IC; however, IC (semicolon before, comma after)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Shackleton gave every man a job; nobody had time to despair. The storm was violent, yet the small boat stayed afloat. Because the captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.","on_screen":"Shackleton gave every man a job; nobody had time to despair. / The storm was violent, yet the small boat stayed afloat. / Because the captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.” That’s not right. We say: “The captain stayed calm, so the crew trusted him.” Comma splice → add a FANBOYS conjunction (or use a semicolon or a period).","on_screen":"✗ The captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.   ✓ The captain stayed calm, so the crew trusted him.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The ship sank, the men survived.\" Is this correct? … Think! … No – it's a comma splice. Great job! Now you can say: I can fix \"The ship sank, the men survived\" in four ways.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can fix \"The ship sank, the men survived\" in four ways.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة المستقلة لها فاعل وفعل وفكرة كاملة، ولا نربط جملتين مستقلتين بلا شيء (run-on) أو بفاصلة فقط (comma splice).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him. — الصحيح: The captain stayed calm, so the crew trusted him.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصحّح The ship sank, the men survived بأربع طرق."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Captain to Remember (editing passage)","body":"Our football team had lost five matches in a row, everyone felt hopeless. Then our captain, Saad, called a meeting he didn't blame anyone. He asked each player for one idea, however, he made the final decision himself. We started training at six in the morning; because the afternoons were too hot. Two months later, we won the regional cup and Saad gave the trophy to our goalkeeper.","word_count":68,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"","options":["The ship sank the men survived.","The ship sank; the men survived.","The ship sank; and, the men survived.","The ship sank, the men survived."],"answer":"The ship sank; the men survived.","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."},{"q":"","options":["The plan was risky; however it was, their only chance.","The plan was risky however it was their only chance.","The plan was risky, however, it was their only chance.","The plan was risky; however, it was their only chance."],"answer":"The plan was risky; however, it was their only chance.","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"","options":["They kept going; although the ice was thick.","They kept going although; the ice was thick.","They kept going. Although the ice was thick.","They kept going, although the ice was thick."],"answer":"They kept going, although the ice was thick.","explanation":"No semicolon before a dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة منقوطة قبل جملة تابعة."},{"q":"Identify the comma splice.","options":["When the captain spoke, everyone listened.","The captain spoke, everyone listened.","The captain spoke, and everyone listened.","The captain spoke; everyone listened."],"answer":"The captain spoke, everyone listened.","explanation":"Comma splice: two independent clauses with only a comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الفاصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"In 1916, Shackleton and five companions sailed the small lifeboat James Caird toward South Georgia ______ the journey took sixteen days.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Island;","Island","Island, and,","Island,"],"answer":"Island;","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."},{"q":"The young volunteers had little experience in organizing large events ______ the festival they planned attracted more than three thousand visitors.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["events, nevertheless,","events, nevertheless","events. Nevertheless,","events nevertheless"],"answer":"events. Nevertheless,","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Fix each sentence. Use the word or mark in brackets.","items":[{"q":"Hamad stayed calm.  +  The team trusted him. (so)","options":[],"answer":"Hamad stayed calm, so the team trusted him.","explanation":"Comma + FANBOYS conjunction.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة + أداة الربط."},{"q":"The road was blocked.  +  We found another route. (; however,)","options":[],"answer":"The road was blocked; however, we found another route.","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"The leader admitted his mistake.  +  Everyone respected him more. (;)","options":[],"answer":"The leader admitted his mistake; everyone respected him more.","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"The team was exhausted, they had been training since dawn.","options":[],"answer":"The team was exhausted; they had been training since dawn.","explanation":", → ;. Comma splice: two independent clauses with only a comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → ;. جملة الفاصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"She prepared carefully, therefore, she won the election.","options":[],"answer":"She prepared carefully; therefore, she won the election.","explanation":", therefore, → ; therefore,. ; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , therefore, → ; therefore,. ظروف الربط."},{"q":"We waited for hours; because the bus had broken down.","options":[],"answer":"We waited for hours, because the bus had broken down.","explanation":"; → ,. No semicolon before a dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ; → ,. لا فاصلة منقوطة قبل جملة تابعة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the leadership story.","items":[{"q":"Our football team had lost five matches in a row, everyone felt hopeless.","options":[],"answer":"Our football team had lost five matches in a row; everyone felt hopeless.","explanation":", → ;. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → ;. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"Then our captain, Saad, called a meeting He didn't blame anyone.","options":[],"answer":"Then our captain, Saad, called a meeting. He didn't blame anyone.","explanation":"(add) → .. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"Then our captain, Saad, called a meeting. he didn't blame anyone.","options":[],"answer":"Then our captain, Saad, called a meeting. He didn't blame anyone.","explanation":"he → He. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: he → He. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"He asked each player for one idea, however, he made the final decision himself.","options":[],"answer":"He asked each player for one idea; however, he made the final decision himself.","explanation":", however, → ; however,. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , however, → ; however,. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"We started training at six in the morning; because the afternoons were too hot.","options":[],"answer":"We started training at six in the morning, because the afternoons were too hot.","explanation":"; → ,. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ; → ,. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"Two months later, we won the regional cup and Saad gave the trophy to our goalkeeper.","options":[],"answer":"Two months later, we won the regional cup, and Saad gave the trophy to our goalkeeper.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write correct boundaries.","items":[{"q":"Write one sentence with a semicolon about a leader.","options":[],"answer":"The coach rarely shouted; his calm voice was enough.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"; however,\" about a difficult situation.","options":[],"answer":"The project was difficult; however, our team finished it on time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Fix this comma splice in two different ways: \"The meeting started late, the speaker was stuck in traffic.\"","options":[],"answer":"The meeting started late because the speaker was stuck in traffic. / The meeting started late; the speaker was stuck in traffic.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"expedition","clue":"a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place"},{"word":"determination","clue":"the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult"},{"word":"initiative","clue":"the ability to act and make decisions without being told"},{"word":"integrity","clue":"the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles"},{"word":"resilient","clue":"able to recover quickly from difficulties"},{"word":"accountable","clue":"responsible for your actions and expected to explain them"},{"word":"crew","clue":"all the people who work on a ship, plane or team"},{"word":"survive","clue":"to stay alive through a dangerous situation"},{"word":"courage","clue":"the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you"},{"word":"morale","clue":"the level of confidence and hope in a group"},{"word":"endure","clue":"to suffer something difficult for a long time"},{"word":"delegate","clue":"to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["The crew was exhausted nobody complained.","The crew was exhausted, nobody complained.","The crew was exhausted but, nobody complained.","The crew was exhausted, but nobody complained."],"answer":"The crew was exhausted, but nobody complained.","explanation":"Comma + FANBOYS conjunction.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة + أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["The storm was violent, nevertheless, the boat stayed afloat.","The storm was violent; nevertheless, the boat stayed afloat.","The storm was violent nevertheless the boat stayed afloat.","The storm was violent; nevertheless the boat, stayed afloat."],"answer":"The storm was violent; nevertheless, the boat stayed afloat.","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"Which option joins two independent clauses with no punctuation at all?","options":["When the bell rang, the students left the hall.","The bell rang the students left the hall.","The bell rang, and the students left the hall.","The bell rang; the students left the hall."],"answer":"The bell rang the students left the hall.","explanation":"Run-on: two independent clauses with no punctuation.","explanation_ar":"الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"","options":["We postponed the trip because the forecast was terrible.","We postponed the trip the forecast was terrible.","We postponed the trip, the forecast was terrible.","We postponed the trip; because the forecast was terrible."],"answer":"We postponed the trip because the forecast was terrible.","explanation":"No semicolon before a dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة منقوطة قبل جملة تابعة."},{"q":"Which of these is a coordinating conjunction (FANBOYS)?","options":["however","therefore","yet","moreover"],"answer":"yet","explanation":"Comma + FANBOYS conjunction.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة + أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["Saad had studied leadership for years; he knew how to motivate people.","Saad had studied leadership for years, he knew how to motivate people.","Saad had studied leadership for years he knew how to motivate people.","Saad had studied leadership for years; and he knew how to motivate people."],"answer":"Saad had studied leadership for years; he knew how to motivate people.","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."},{"q":"Marie Curie was the first person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences ______ she won in physics in 1903 and in chemistry in 1911.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["sciences;","sciences, and,","sciences,","sciences"],"answer":"sciences;","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."},{"q":"The new student council president had never led a team before ______ she quickly earned the respect of every member.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["before however","before, however,","before; however,","before, however"],"answer":"before; however,","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"Ibn Battuta began his travels in 1325 at the age of twenty-one ______ he did not return home for almost thirty years.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["twenty-one","twenty-one,","twenty-one, and","twenty-one and,"],"answer":"twenty-one, and","explanation":"Comma + FANBOYS conjunction.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة + أداة الربط."},{"q":"What is the problem with \"The leader listened carefully, then she made a decision.\"?","options":["It needs a question mark.","It's a fragment.","Nothing is wrong.","It's a comma splice."],"answer":"It's a comma splice.","explanation":"Comma splice: two independent clauses with only a comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الفاصلة الخاطئة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Leaders and Leadership” that shows sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Leaders and Leadership” that shows sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause in action"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Fixing Run-Ons and Comma Splices: Periods, Conjunctions and Semicolons (SAT Boundaries)”. Let’s learn sentence boundaries: run-ons and comma splices; four fixes (period, comma + FANBOYS, semicolon, subordinating conjunction); semicolon + conjunctive adverb + comma (; however,); no semicolon before a dependent clause together. Two independent clauses (each with its own subject and verb and a complete idea) can't be joined with nothing (a run-on) or with only a comma (a comma splice): (not: The ship sank the men survived.) (not: The ship sank, the men survived.) These are the most common errors tested in the SAT Boundaries questions. Two independent clauses (each with its own subject and verb and a complete idea) can't be joined with nothing (a run-on) or with only a comma (a comma splice): (not: The ship sank the men survived.) (not: The ship sank, the men survived.) These are the most common errors tested in the SAT Boundaries questions. Four correct fixes: (1) period: The ship sank. The men survived. (2) comma + FANBOYS (for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so): The ship sank, but the men survived. (3) semicolon for closely related ideas: The ship sank; the men survived. (4) subordinating conjunction: Although the ship sank, the men survived. Here are some examples. Shackleton gave every man a job; nobody had time to despair. The storm was violent, yet the small boat stayed afloat. Because the captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him. Be careful! Some learners say: “The captain stayed calm, the crew trusted him.” That’s not right. We say: “The captain stayed calm, so the crew trusted him.” Comma splice → add a FANBOYS conjunction (or use a semicolon or a period). Quick check: \"The ship sank, the men survived.\" Is this correct? … Think! … No – it's a comma splice. Great job! Now you can say: I can fix \"The ship sank, the men survived\" in four ways.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5","title":"A Leader I Have Worked With: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to tell a leadership story with accurate narrative tenses.","Students will be able to write a leadership narrative with correct boundaries and choose logical transitions and effective sentences in SAT-style tasks.","I can tell the story of a leader I know.","I can choose the best transition for a sentence."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من رواية قصة عن القيادة بأزمنة سردية دقيقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة قصة عن القيادة بحدود جمل صحيحة واختيار الروابط المنطقية والجمل الفعّالة في مهام بنمط SAT.","أستطيع أن أروي قصة قائد أعرفه.","أستطيع أن أختار أفضل رابط لجملة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"expedition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən/","definition":"a long, organized journey to a distant or dangerous place","arabic":"بعثة استكشافية","example":"The expedition to the South Pole took two years.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"crew","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kru/","definition":"all the people who work on a ship, plane or team","arabic":"طاقم","example":"The captain and his crew sailed through the storm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"survive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɚˈvaɪv/","definition":"to stay alive through a dangerous situation","arabic":"ينجو / يبقى على قيد الحياة","example":"All the climbers survived the avalanche.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"courage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɝədʒ/","definition":"the ability to do something difficult or dangerous without fear stopping you","arabic":"شجاعة","example":"It takes courage to admit a mistake.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"morale","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mɚˈæl/","definition":"the level of confidence and hope in a group","arabic":"الروح المعنوية","example":"The coach's speech lifted the team's morale.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"resilient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪljənt/","definition":"able to recover quickly from difficulties","arabic":"صامد / مرن","example":"Resilient people don't give up after a failure.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"endure","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɛndˈjʊr/","definition":"to suffer something difficult for a long time","arabic":"يتحمّل / يصمد","example":"The sailors endured months of freezing cold.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"determination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˌtɝməˈneɪʃən/","definition":"the quality of continuing to try even when it is difficult","arabic":"عزيمة / إصرار","example":"With determination, she finished the race.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"delegate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdɛləˌɡeɪt/","definition":"to give part of your work or responsibility to someone else","arabic":"يفوّض","example":"A good captain delegates tasks to the team.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"collaborate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlæbɚˌeɪt/","definition":"to work together with others on a project","arabic":"يتعاون","example":"The two schools collaborated on a science project.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"initiative","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪˈnɪʃətɪv/","definition":"the ability to act and make decisions without being told","arabic":"المبادرة","example":"Faisal took the initiative and organized the event.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"integrity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈtɛɡrəti/","definition":"the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles","arabic":"النزاهة","example":"Leaders with integrity keep their promises.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vision","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɪʒən/","definition":"a clear idea of what you want to achieve in the future","arabic":"رؤية","example":"Saudi Vision 2030 is a plan for the future of the country.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mentor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛnˌtɔr/","definition":"an experienced person who advises and guides a younger person","arabic":"مرشد / موجّه","example":"My older cousin is my mentor in programming.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"accountable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈkaʊntəbəl/","definition":"responsible for your actions and expected to explain them","arabic":"مسؤول / خاضع للمساءلة","example":"Every team member is accountable for his part.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: narrative tenses including the past perfect continuous, past perfect simple vs continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, and correct sentence boundaries.\nSAT Expression of Ideas questions ask you to choose the most logical transition (however, therefore, for example, in addition, instead, as a result) or the sentence that best uses notes to achieve a goal (rhetorical synthesis). Read the sentences before and after the blank, decide the relationship (contrast, cause–effect, example, addition), and then choose.\n✔ past simple • past continuous • past perfect • past perfect continuous\n✔ delegate, collaborate, initiative, integrity, vision, morale\n✔ IC; IC • IC; however, IC • IC, so IC\n✔ transitions: contrast (however), result (therefore), example (for example), addition (moreover)","examples":["The team had been practicing for weeks when the captain got injured.","While we were waiting for the results, nobody spoke.","By the end of the season, they had won twelve matches.","The captain took the initiative; he called a team meeting.","The plan seemed impossible; however, the team believed in it.","He had trained harder than anyone; as a result, he was chosen as captain.","Leaders must stay calm. For example, Shackleton kept his crew busy with routines.","She underestimated the challenge, but she never gave up."],"common_errors":["✗ Hamad led the team for two years when I joined. → ✓ Hamad had been leading the team for two years when I joined. (Duration up to a past moment.)","✗ We were exhausted, nobody wanted to start again. → ✓ We were exhausted; nobody wanted to start again. (Comma splice → semicolon.)","✗ The robot stopped. Therefore, we celebrated. → ✓ The robot stopped. However, we didn't give up. (Choose the transition that fits the logic (contrast, not result).)"],"arabic":"نراجع الأزمنة السردية والماضي التام المستمر ومفردات القيادة والبادئات وحدود الجمل.\nأسئلة Expression of Ideas في SAT تطلب اختيار الرابط المنطقي (however للتضاد، therefore للنتيجة، for example للمثال، moreover للإضافة) أو الجملة التي تستخدم الملاحظات لتحقيق هدف محدد.\nاقرأ ما قبل الفراغ وما بعده، وحدّد العلاقة بين الجملتين، ثم اختر."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Leader I Have Worked With: Language in Use”. Let’s learn narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L08-U1-LS5 | A Leader I Have Worked With: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Leadership story circle: each student tells a 1-minute story about a leader (a captain, a teacher, a parent, a historical figure). Listeners note one past perfect continuous sentence and one leadership word they heard, then ask one question.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: narrative tenses including the past perfect continuous, past perfect simple vs continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, and correct sentence boundaries. SAT Expression of Ideas questions ask you to choose the most logical transition (however, therefore, for example, in addition, instead, as a result) or the sentence that best uses notes to achieve a goal (rhetorical synthesis). Read the sentences before and after the blank, decide the relationship (contrast, cause–effect, example, addition), and then choose.","on_screen":"✔ past simple • past continuous • past perfect • past perfect continuous • ✔ delegate, collaborate, initiative, integrity, vision, morale • ✔ IC; IC • IC; however, IC • IC, so IC","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The team had been practicing for weeks when the captain got injured. While we were waiting for the results, nobody spoke. By the end of the season, they had won twelve matches.","on_screen":"The team had been practicing for weeks when the captain got injured. / While we were waiting for the results, nobody spoke. / By the end of the season, they had won twelve matches.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Hamad led the team for two years when I joined.” That’s not right. We say: “Hamad had been leading the team for two years when I joined.” Duration up to a past moment.","on_screen":"✗ Hamad led the team for two years when I joined.   ✓ Hamad had been leading the team for two years when I joined.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “We were exhausted, nobody wanted to start again.”? … Think! … It should be “We were exhausted; nobody wanted to start again.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell the story of a leader I know.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can tell the story of a leader I know.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الأزمنة السردية والماضي التام المستمر ومفردات القيادة والبادئات وحدود الجمل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Hamad led the team for two years when I joined. — الصحيح: Hamad had been leading the team for two years when I joined.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أروي قصة قائد أعرفه."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf","body":"When I joined the school robotics team, our captain, Hamad, had been leading the team for two years.\nHe had never won a national competition; nevertheless, he had built a team that trusted each other.\nOne evening, while we were preparing for the regional final, our robot suddenly stopped working.\nWe had been testing it for six hours, and everyone was exhausted; nobody wanted to start again.\nHamad didn't blame anyone. Instead, he delegated small tasks and reminded us of our vision.\nBy midnight, we had found the problem, and two days later, we won the final.\nHamad showed me that a true leader stays calm and makes everyone feel accountable.","word_count":111,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's story. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Hamad had been leading the team for two years when Yusuf joined.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Hamad had already won a national competition.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The robot stopped working while the team was preparing for the regional final.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The team had been testing the robot for six hours.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Hamad blamed the programmers for the problem.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The team won the final two days later.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Night Our Robot Stopped – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Hamad ___ the team for two years when Yusuf joined.","options":["has been leading","had been leading","was led","leads"],"answer":"had been leading","explanation":"Narrative tense choice.","explanation_ar":"اختيار الزمن السردي."},{"q":"While they ___ for the final, the robot stopped working.","options":["were preparing","prepare","have prepared","had prepared all"],"answer":"were preparing","explanation":"Narrative tense choice.","explanation_ar":"اختيار الزمن السردي."},{"q":"Hamad ___ small tasks to each member.","options":["survived","collaborated","delegated","endured"],"answer":"delegated","explanation":"Leadership word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القيادة."},{"q":"","options":["We were exhausted; and nobody wanted to start again.","We were exhausted, nobody wanted to start again.","We were exhausted nobody wanted to start again.","We were exhausted; nobody wanted to start again."],"answer":"We were exhausted; nobody wanted to start again.","explanation":"Sentence boundary.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."},{"q":"Hamad had never won a national title. ______ he had built a team that trusted each other.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Therefore,","For example,","Nevertheless,","Similarly,"],"answer":"Nevertheless,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"The robot had stopped working the night before the final. ______ the team stayed up until midnight to fix it.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["However,","As a result,","Likewise,","For instance,"],"answer":"As a result,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Plan your leadership story.","items":[{"q":"The leader and the situation: ___","options":[],"answer":"My uncle Khalid, the manager of a small bakery during Ramadan","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Background (past continuous): ___","options":[],"answer":"Customers were waiting in long lines, and the ovens were working nonstop.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Duration before a key moment (past perfect continuous): ___","options":[],"answer":"The workers had been baking since three in the morning when one oven broke.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What the leader did (past simple + leadership word): ___","options":[],"answer":"My uncle stayed calm and delegated new tasks to every worker.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A sentence with a semicolon or \"; however,\": ___","options":[],"answer":"The day was exhausting; however, every customer went home with bread.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your leadership narrative.","items":[{"q":"Plan: leader, setting, problem, how long, the leader's action, result, lesson.","options":[],"answer":"Ms. Huda; school play; the main actor got sick; we had been rehearsing for six weeks; she gave his role to a shy student and coached him; the play was a success; leaders see potential in people","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your narrative in 8–9 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Last spring, our class was preparing for the school play. We had been rehearsing for six weeks when our main actor got sick. Everyone was panicking; the play was only three days away. Our teacher, Ms. Huda, didn't cancel the show. Instead, she took the initiative and gave the role to Adam, who was very shy. She had been watching him in rehearsals, and she knew he had memorized every line. She coached him every afternoon; as a result, he grew more confident. On the night of the play, Adam was brilliant. Ms. Huda taught me that great leaders see potential in people.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: tenses? run-ons or comma splices? semicolons and conjunctive adverbs? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Everyone was panicking, the play was only three days away\" to \"Everyone was panicking; the play was only three days away.\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"expedition","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"crew","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"survive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"courage","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"morale","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"resilient","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"endure","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"determination","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"delegate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"collaborate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"initiative","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"integrity","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vision","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mentor","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"accountable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The volunteers ___ for five hours when the rain started.","options":["had been working","work","were worked","have been working"],"answer":"had been working","explanation":"Narrative tense choice.","explanation_ar":"اختيار الزمن السردي."},{"q":"By the end of the campaign, the team ___ 1,000 trees.","options":["had planted","had been planting","has planted","plants"],"answer":"had planted","explanation":"Narrative tense choice.","explanation_ar":"اختيار الزمن السردي."},{"q":"A leader who keeps his promises shows ___.","options":["morale","integrity","expedition","initiative"],"answer":"integrity","explanation":"Leadership word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القيادة."},{"q":"","options":["The captain was injured, however, the team won the match.","The captain was injured; however the team, won the match.","The captain was injured; however, the team won the match.","The captain was injured however the team won the match."],"answer":"The captain was injured; however, the team won the match.","explanation":"Sentence boundary.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."},{"q":"Strong leaders listen before they act. ______ Shackleton asked his men about their fears before he made important decisions.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Nevertheless,","However,","For example,","In contrast,"],"answer":"For example,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"The coach expected the team to struggle in its first season. ______ the players won eight of their first ten matches.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Therefore,","Similarly,","For example,","Instead,"],"answer":"Instead,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Fatima al-Fihri used her inheritance to found al-Qarawiyyin in Fez in 859.\n• Al-Qarawiyyin began as a mosque.\n• It became a famous center of learning.\n• It is often described as the oldest existing university in the world.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize al-Qarawiyyin's importance today. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Founded in 859, al-Qarawiyyin is often described as the oldest existing university in the world.","Fatima al-Fihri used her inheritance to build a mosque in Fez.","Al-Qarawiyyin began as a mosque in the city of Fez.","In 859, a woman named Fatima al-Fihri had an inheritance."],"answer":"Founded in 859, al-Qarawiyyin is often described as the oldest existing university in the world.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis (using notes for a goal).","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Ernest Shackleton led the Endurance expedition (1914–1917).\n• The ship was crushed by ice in 1915.\n• Shackleton kept his men busy with jobs and routines.\n• All twenty-eight men survived.\n\nThe student wants to highlight Shackleton's leadership. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In 1915, the ship Endurance was crushed by ice.","The Endurance expedition took place between 1914 and 1917.","By keeping his men busy with jobs and routines, Shackleton made sure that all twenty-eight survived after their ship was crushed by ice.","Shackleton's ship was called Endurance, and it was crushed in 1915."],"answer":"By keeping his men busy with jobs and routines, Shackleton made sure that all twenty-eight survived after their ship was crushed by ice.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis (using notes for a goal).","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad had been captain for two years, he knew every player's strengths.","Hamad had been captain for two years, so he knew every player's strengths.","Hamad was being captain for two years, so he knew every player's strengths.","Hamad had been captain for two years so, he knew every player's strengths."],"answer":"Hamad had been captain for two years, so he knew every player's strengths.","explanation":"Sentence boundary.","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a leadership narrative:","options":["We were rehearsing for weeks when our lead actor fell ill, however, our teacher refused to cancel the show.","We have been rehearsing for weeks when our lead actor fell ill; however our teacher refused to cancel the show.","We had rehearsed for weeks when our lead actor falls ill, our teacher refused to cancel the show.","We had been rehearsing for weeks when our lead actor fell ill; however, our teacher refused to cancel the show."],"answer":"We had been rehearsing for weeks when our lead actor fell ill; however, our teacher refused to cancel the show.","explanation":"Narrative tense choice.","explanation_ar":"اختيار الزمن السردي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A school robotics competition at night: the team exhausted around a broken robot, captain Hamad calmly pointing to a whiteboard with tasks for each member; a second panel shows the team holding a trophy. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school robotics competition at night: the team exhausted around a broken robot, captain Hamad calmly pointing to a whiteboard with tasks for each member; a second panel shows the team holding a trophy"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Leaders and Leadership”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Leaders and Leadership”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L08-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS5-T1","script":"When I joined the school robotics team, our captain, Hamad, had been leading the team for two years. He had never won a national competition; nevertheless, he had built a team that trusted each other. One evening, while we were preparing for the regional final, our robot suddenly stopped working. We had been testing it for six hours, and everyone was exhausted; nobody wanted to start again. Hamad didn't blame anyone. Instead, he delegated small tasks and reminded us of our vision. By midnight, we had found the problem, and two days later, we won the final. Hamad showed me that a true leader stays calm and makes everyone feel accountable.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L08-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Leader I Have Worked With: Language in Use”. Let’s learn narrative tenses and the past perfect continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, sentence boundaries; SAT transitions and rhetorical synthesis (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Leadership story circle: each student tells a 1-minute story about a leader (a captain, a teacher, a parent, a historical figure). Listeners note one past perfect continuous sentence and one leadership word they heard, then ask one question. Today you use all of Unit 1: narrative tenses including the past perfect continuous, past perfect simple vs continuous, leadership vocabulary and prefixes, and correct sentence boundaries. SAT Expression of Ideas questions ask you to choose the most logical transition (however, therefore, for example, in addition, instead, as a result) or the sentence that best uses notes to achieve a goal (rhetorical synthesis). Read the sentences before and after the blank, decide the relationship (contrast, cause–effect, example, addition), and then choose. Here are some examples. The team had been practicing for weeks when the captain got injured. While we were waiting for the results, nobody spoke. By the end of the season, they had won twelve matches. Be careful! Some learners say: “Hamad led the team for two years when I joined.” That’s not right. We say: “Hamad had been leading the team for two years when I joined.” Duration up to a past moment. Quick check: what is wrong with “We were exhausted, nobody wanted to start again.”? … Think! … It should be “We were exhausted; nobody wanted to start again.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell the story of a leader I know.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"While the explorers ___ across the ice, they heard a loud crack.","options":["walk","have been walking","were walking","had walked for"],"answer":"were walking","explanation":"Background or action in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"By the time help arrived, the miners ___ underground for three days.","options":["were trapping","had been trapped","have been trapped","are trapped"],"answer":"had been trapped","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"The leader ___ his team for years, so he knew them well.","options":["had been knowing","has been knowing","had known","was knowing"],"answer":"had known","explanation":"State verbs → past perfect simple.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← الماضي التام البسيط."},{"q":"After the captain ___ his speech, the players walked onto the field.","options":["finishes","has finished","had been finishing for","had finished"],"answer":"had finished","explanation":"Earlier completed event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"Hillary and Norgay ______ toward the summit for hours when they finally saw the top of the world on May 29, 1953.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["are climbing","had been climbing","climb","have been climbing"],"answer":"had been climbing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."},{"q":"By the end of the drive, the club ___ 300 blankets for refugees.","options":["collects","had been collecting","had collected","has collected"],"answer":"had collected","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"His clothes were muddy because he ___ in the garden.","options":["had worked three","had been working","has worked","works"],"answer":"had been working","explanation":"Visible effect of an activity → continuous.","explanation_ar":"الأثر الظاهر ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["How many interviews had she given before the election?","How many interviews had she been giving before the election?","How many interviews did she gave before the election?","How many interviews has she been giving before the election?"],"answer":"How many interviews had she given before the election?","explanation":"how many / how much / numbers → simple.","explanation_ar":"الأعداد ← البسيط."},{"q":"The new captain lifted the team's ___ with a powerful speech.","options":["integrity","morale","moral","mentor"],"answer":"morale","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"She didn't wait to be told; she ___ the initiative.","options":["made","gave","did","took"],"answer":"took","explanation":"Leadership collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة."},{"q":"He ___ the difficulty of the exam and didn't study enough.","options":["misbehaved","overestimated","underestimated","reconsidered"],"answer":"underestimated","explanation":"Use the prefix to find or form the meaning.","explanation_ar":"البادئة."},{"q":"Our ___ approach helped every member share ideas.","options":["collaborator","collaboration","collaborative","collaborate"],"answer":"collaborative","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Despite losing her first two elections, the candidate remained ______ and won the third one by a large margin.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["determined","reluctant","indifferent","discouraged"],"answer":"determined","explanation":"Choose the leadership word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Which of these joins two complete sentences with only a comma?","options":["The team lost, the fans were disappointed.","Because the team lost, the fans were disappointed.","The team lost, and the fans were disappointed.","The team lost; the fans were disappointed."],"answer":"The team lost, the fans were disappointed.","explanation":"Comma splice: two independent clauses with only a comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الفاصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"","options":["The road was closed; therefore we took, a longer route.","The road was closed, therefore, we took a longer route.","The road was closed therefore we took a longer route.","The road was closed; therefore, we took a longer route."],"answer":"The road was closed; therefore, we took a longer route.","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"","options":["We stayed indoors the dust storm was severe.","We stayed indoors because the dust storm was severe.","We stayed indoors; because the dust storm was severe.","We stayed indoors, the dust storm was severe."],"answer":"We stayed indoors because the dust storm was severe.","explanation":"No semicolon before a dependent clause.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة منقوطة قبل جملة تابعة."},{"q":"Al-Khwarizmi worked at the House of Wisdom in Baghdad ______ his books on mathematics were later translated into Latin.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Baghdad, and,","Baghdad,","Baghdad","Baghdad;"],"answer":"Baghdad;","explanation":"Semicolon between two independent clauses.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة المنقوطة."},{"q":"The young team had little money for equipment ______ its creative design won first prize at the national competition.\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["equipment, however","equipment, however,","equipment however","equipment; however,"],"answer":"equipment; however,","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"Good leaders admit their mistakes. ______ when her plan failed, the principal apologized to the staff and asked for their ideas.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["However,","Nevertheless,","For example,","In contrast,"],"answer":"For example,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"The engineers expected the bridge to take five years to build. ______ it was finished in three.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Instead,","Similarly,","Therefore,","For instance,"],"answer":"Instead,","explanation":"Logical transition.","explanation_ar":"الرابط المنطقي."},{"q":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Al-Biruni (973–1048) was a scholar from Central Asia.\n• He studied astronomy, mathematics and geography.\n• He calculated the size of the Earth.\n• His result was close to modern measurements.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize the accuracy of Al-Biruni's work. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Al-Biruni studied astronomy, mathematics and geography.","Al-Biruni was a scholar from Central Asia.","Al-Biruni, who lived from 973 to 1048, studied astronomy.","Al-Biruni calculated the size of the Earth, and his result was close to modern measurements."],"answer":"Al-Biruni calculated the size of the Earth, and his result was close to modern measurements.","explanation":"Rhetorical synthesis (using notes for a goal).","explanation_ar":"التركيب البلاغي."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a leadership story:","options":["The crew had been drifting on the ice for months; nevertheless, Shackleton kept their spirits high.","The crew have been drifting on the ice for months; nevertheless Shackleton kept their spirits high.","The crew drifted on the ice for months, nevertheless, Shackleton kept their spirits high.","The crew had been drift on the ice for months, Shackleton kept their spirits high."],"answer":"The crew had been drifting on the ice for months; nevertheless, Shackleton kept their spirits high.","explanation":"; however, / ; therefore, (conjunctive adverbs).","explanation_ar":"ظروف الربط."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the coach had been training us since june, we were ready.\"","options":["the coach had been training us since June; so we were ready.","The coach had been training us since June, so we were ready.","The coach had been training us since june, so we were ready.","The coach had been training us since June, we were ready."],"answer":"The coach had been training us since June, so we were ready.","explanation":"Comma splice: two independent clauses with only a comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الفاصلة الخاطئة."},{"q":"\"They had been sailing for sixteen days when they saw land.\" Which event came first?","options":["the sailing","seeing land","They happened at the same time.","We can't tell."],"answer":"the sailing","explanation":"Duration up to a past moment → had been + -ing.","explanation_ar":"المدة حتى لحظة ماضية ← had been + ing."}],"theme_ar":"القادة والقيادة","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل شخصًا ما قائدًا عظيمًا؟","can_do":"I can tell stories with narrative tenses including the past perfect continuous, choose between the past perfect simple and continuous, use leadership vocabulary and prefixes, and fix run-ons and comma splices with periods, conjunctions and semicolons.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أروي القصص بالأزمنة السردية ومنها الماضي التام المستمر، وأختار بين الماضي التام البسيط والمستمر، وأستخدم مفردات القيادة والبادئات، وأصحّح الجمل المتصلة الخاطئة وجمل الفاصلة الخاطئة بالنقطة وأدوات الربط والفاصلة المنقوطة."});
